<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Álvaro I of Kongo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1587">1587</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Álvaro I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> from 1568 to 1587. Early in his reign invaders known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaga">Jaga</a> overran the kingdom and drove him from his capital, São <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>, to an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a>, and he was restored in the early 1570s with the help of Portuguese troops sent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-tome">São Tomé</a>. He promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, and his reign saw the Portuguese establish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> to the south in 1576.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alvaro-i-of-kongo.jpg" alt="Álvaro I of Kongo" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Congoking.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
